6400 Granted by Cesar on 2026-10-14 (option B of question direct-budget-q1 on the owner's
dashboard, issue #101); the limit and the rule wording were set by the owner (Jayson) on
2026-10-14. The rule: a case whose cost comes from a compiler defect with an open issue, until
the case fits 4 300M.
Cause: a browser/direct/ page is four builds in one case (browser-direct and browser-tea, dev and
release), and Http.jsonBody reaches the core/Schema library interpreter, which the release
specialiser processes in both release builds (issue #105).
Size: on the gate's host (Zen 2) the case is 4 942M, and 5 809M when Node runs the pages.
PR #104's reference CPU, x86_64_v3+sha, counts within 5M of Zen 2. The limit is 5 809M plus 10%.
Remove when the case fits 4 300M without this file.
